The shirt wouldn't be that helpful, AC -20 is more than fine to go
deep into Gehennom.  MR, on the other hand, is a high priority.  You
should be fine to tackle the castle, where the storerooms/dragons/wand
will net you MR (and you should be able to fill in any other missing
goodies at that point).   Using the drawbridge as a guillotine, even a
low-level character can fairly safely get the wand (assuming you have
some way to burn Elbereth, though it's doable with just dust-E).  I'd
be diving for the castle, and definitely be willing to zap /digging or
whatever if a particularly nasty foe shows up along the way--once
you've done the castle, which is only a few levels past Medusa at
most, you'll be well equipped to come back and deal with it.


